RUN: %PLC -c --fpic "%S/lib/*.st" -o %t.lib.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i "%S/lib/*.st" "%S/app/*.st" %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: %COMPILE --generate-external-constructors -i "%S/lib/*.st" "%S/app/*.st" %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s

The library in lib/ declares interfaces whose methods and properties use types
with constructors: STRING[n], WSTRING[n], ARRAY, subrange, ARRAY OF interface
and POINTER TO parameters, inputs with default values, STRING[n] and ARRAY
return values, VAR_OUTPUT and VAR_IN_OUT strings, REFERENCE TO and REF_TO
parameters, STRING[n] and ARRAY properties with getters and setters, methods
of extended interfaces (also of an interface that extends two), a WSTRING[n]
input with a default value and a REFERENCE TO interface parameter.
IDeclaredOnly has no implementor and adds an inline enum parameter, inline
nested arrays, a REFERENCE TO return value, an ARRAY[*] OF STRING[n] parameter
and pointers to inline arrays.
The library is compiled to its own object. The program in app/ includes it,
links that object, and calls through the interfaces into library types and into
program types. Only the library object may define the constructors of these
parameter types.

